welcome back to new rockstars i'm  whitney van laningham and holy nine  hells we're getting a dnd movie as a  tabaxi arcane trickster myself i can't  wait to see my favorite tabletop rpg  coming to the silver screen you hear  that popular kids from my high school  dungeons and dragons is hot now written  and directed by jonathan goldstein and  jon francis daily aka the writing duo  behind spider-man homecoming this movie  is definitely something that i think  y'all will enjoy even if you're not a d  d super fan yet today i'm taking you  frame by frame through the new dungeons  and dragons honor among thieves trailer  point out all the d in details you might  have missed the trailer opens on  neverwinter a bustling city of craftsmen  merchants and gardeners in northwest  faerun also known as the jewel of the  north front and center you can see  castle never home of neverwinter's  rulers interestingly the movie has added  a coliseum to its landscape a structure  that doesn't exist on any official maps  of neverwinter chris pine a human bard  named edgin introduces their party as a  team of thieves made up of michelle  rodriguez a barbarian named holga  justice smith a half elf sorcerer named  simon and sophia lillis a tiefling druid  named doric peep that white dragon  statue as the party walks through the  market square it actually comes to life  later on in the trailer in the  background of this scene you can see  neverwinter's blue banner emblazoned  with three snowflakes next the party  makes their way through the underdark  expansive network of caverns tunnels and  passageways that lie underground the  city they make their way through looks  to be crackle stuff also known as the  city of blades a subterranean fire lit  home to an underground race of dwarves  called the duergar these grave dwarves  are known to be cynical and tyrannical  and are only happy when they cause the  suffering of others the statues we see  aligning the chamber are during our  priests who display psionic powers in  some d lore reggie gene page's paladin  named zenk pulls a golden helmet out of  an intricate puzzle contraption it was  revealed in an exclusive sdcc clip that  this item is called the helm of  destruction the mechanical contraption  that holds it is covered in death rooms  that likely detail how to open it in  dwarvish language the dragon we see  attacking the battlefield is a black  dragon the most brutally destructive and  solitary of all chromatic dragons these  guys are known for their ambush style  combat and their use of acid breath  which might be the gross deadly barf  coming out of the dragon's face hole as  edgan ushers his fellow adventurers to  safety you can see that he's wearing a  harper pool signifying his former  membership to a semi-secret organization  of people whose mission is to preserve  art minimize the destruction of animal  and plant life fight villainy and  protect the freedoms of those around  them the harpers mainly operate out of  northern faerun confirming that this d d  story takes place within the forgotten  realm setting the door he leads them  through also has the same symbol  inscribed on it so perhaps this is a  harper safehouse of some kind although  several important deities in d d lore  support the harpers they also have  equally powerful enemies such as the red  wizards of fey one of whom we see here  holding a glowing red horn the red  wizards of they are a magical cult of  demonologists dedicated to creating a  world of un-death filled with  spiritually reanimated corpses i think  that this artifact could possibly be the  drachorn the horn of a red dragon gifted  to dragonkind by tiamat the evil  five-headed dragon goddess as the queen  of all chromatic dragons she created the  drac horn as a means to call any  chromatic dragon within two thousand  miles however like i said the red  wizards of they are super into  necromancy so this could be a tool  unique to this movie that falls more in  line with those characters zombie  hobbies interestingly though there have  been plots by red wizards to turn living  dragons into dracoliches so that they  can command hordes of dragon zombies so  maybe the horn is being used in honor  among thieves for a little bit of both  behind the red horn is an alchemy jug a  magic container that produces any liquid  you desire i use mine for teriyaki sauce  the red wizard using the horn in the  next shot is likely sastam an incredibly  powerful lich and one of the eight  zulkers aka powerful rulers of thing he  was the ruler of necromancy and leader  of a massive army of undead soldiers i  wouldn't be surprised if this dude was  the greatest evil ever known that edgin  and his crew unleashed it seems that his  followers are blocking these civilians  escape using spell wall of force next we  get our first look at paddington 2's  very own hugh grant grant's character is  a sneaky rogue named forge fitzwilliams  who like this red wizard appears to be  on the party's side at this point in the  movie the red wizard here is likely  casting the spell slow the woods we see  here could possibly be the outer rim of  the dread ring in neverwinter wood  forged by liches dread rings or  necromantic ritual sights slash  fortresses for the red wizards of fae  the space surrounding a dread ring oozes  with evil be it through a swamp of blood  or a dusting of ash this evil aura may  be what gives the trees in this trailer  their lovely crimson hue also say hello  to this giant spider the wintry town  where edgin and holga agree to talk over  a drink is most likely located in  icewinddale home to tough pioneers and  barbarians in the northernmost region of  faerun on a snowy tundra based on the  trees i'd say that this is the town of  lonely wood surrounded by the lonely  wood forest when we see them handcuffed  a few moments later they could be at  revel's end the cliffside prison near  lonelywood this cracked snow-covered  landscape is the spine of the world the  mountain range that stretches across  northern faerun while holga forges what  looks like a home-brewed magma axe zenk  wields a dagger sword a magical weapon  exclusive to this movie simon uses the  helmet of destruction while casting  thunder waves a spell that sweeps a wave  of thunderous force out from under you  the glowing orb we see hovering in the  next shot could be a drift globe a  floating light that can either glow as  dim as a flashlight or as bright as  daylight depending on what the user  needs it for when we finally meet doric  she uses wild shape to transform from a  horse into an owl bear which looks cool  as [ __ ] but it's technically inaccurate  not to be a well actually but according  to 5e rules druids can't become angle  bears using wild shape likewise the  spell she uses a few moments later to  travel between worlds is called  dimension door which druids typically  don't have access to so doric is either  a brand new subclass or the director  master is down with the rule of cool  it's like a dungeon master but he  directs the movie as simon confirms the  creature's identity check out his  satchel it looks to me like it could be  the bag of holding a small sack that  opens to extra dimensional space  allowing its user to carry up to 500  pounds the volcanic mountain in the next  shot is mount houghton now a volcano in  the crags mountain range deep in the  neverwinter woods next we meet some cool  characters with some cool spells jason  wong's character drallis casts the  cantrip green flame blade daisy heads  red wizard casts a lightning bolt  emitting blue electric energy outside  the coliseum simon casts the protection  spell globe of invulnerability which  protects you up to a 10 foot radius  inside the coliseum our heroic gang of  thieves prepare for battle we get a much  better look at forge fitzwilliams here  in the maze holga approaches one of the  most classic and signature d d monsters  the mimic this monster shape-shifts into  normal household objects or enticing  chests of gold to attract unsuspecting  prey edgin simon and doric narrowly  dodge an attacking displacer beast by  diving headfirst into a gelatinous cube  displacer beasts are magical  panther-like creatures with six legs and  tentacles sprouting from their shoulders  their magic can bend light making  themselves displace aka appear closer or  farther away than they actually are but  diving head first into a gelatinous cube  ain't no walk in winterfell either these  suckers are acidic and typically absorb  and dissolve their prey extremely  quickly see that skeleton guy down there  that guy stayed in there a little too  long simon casts ice knife in the battle  arena a spell that flings a shard of ice  that explodes on impact whether you hit  your target or miss i've seen some fans  speculating that these projectiles could  also be magic missiles but those never  miss their intended target these blasts  don't seem as precise as magic missiles  should be but who knows like i said  earlier the rule of cool seems to apply  to a lot of scenarios in this movie  daisy head's red wizard uses misty step  to dodge the owl bear a spell that  creates a plume of mist around its  caster allowing them to teleport up to  30 feet to an unoccupied space the mist  is usually silver and not red but i  actually like that they're using an  alternate color here to display her they  powers the best part of this trailer  however is when we meet thember chowd  the chunkiest tubbiest red dragon in d d  lore his job is to protect the dory  guard of grackle stug in the underdark  and look i know that he's a chaotic evil  and that he barbecues and eats anyone  who disagrees with him but look at that  cute chubby little bunny oh love him  even if he's a bad guy he's like a thick  dangerous pug the reason why this guy  has a low belly is because he powers  grackle stugs forges with his flame  breath and in return the duraguard feed  him whatever he wants and bring him  treasure as you can see here he's trying  to eat chris pine because chris pine is  a goddamn snack finally we get to see  what we really all came here for a bard  strumming his loot and doing a jaunty  little jig but listen up doric edgin is  way more powerful than he looks the bard  in my campaign has saved our asses with  music more times than i've slayed a  monster with my custom gnomish  engineered dagger claws these are just  some of the easter eggs that i found in  the honor among thieves trailer but i  want my fellow dnd nerds to let me know  what i missed in the comments but d  indeed there's always new lore to learn  follow me on instagram and twitter  whitney puppy follow new rockstar  subscribe to rockstars for more analysis  of everything you love and thanks for  watching bye  [Music]  you

